        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): guard parseRequest JSON.parse against malformed WebSocket data",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`extensions/codex/src/app-server/sandbox-exec-server/json-rpc.ts:30` calls bare `JSON.parse(text)` in `parseRequest()` when parsing WebSocket raw data into JSON-RPC request objects. Malformed data from a sandbox exec server WebSocket connection → raw `SyntaxError` instead of descriptive validation error.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `json-rpc.ts`: wrap `JSON.parse(text)` in try/catch, throw `Error(\"JSON-RPC request body is not valid JSON.\")` instead of raw SyntaxError\n- `test/_proof_codex_sandbox_json_rpc_guard.mts`: standalone proof script (7/7 PASS)\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal | AI-assisted\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx test/_proof_codex_sandbox_json_rpc_guard.mts\n\n[1] malformed JSON Buffer → descriptive Error\n  PASS  throws Error (not SyntaxError)\n  PASS  message includes \"not valid JSON\"\n\n[2] valid JSON-RPC request → returns correctly\n  PASS  no error thrown\n  PASS  returns object\n  PASS  method is \"tools/call\"\n\n[3] empty Buffer → throws Error\n  PASS  throws Error for empty data\n\n[4] valid JSON non-object → requireObject validation\n  PASS  throws Error for non-object JSON\n\n==================================================\n  Passed: 7  Failed: 0  Total: 7\n==================================================\n```\n\nBefore: `parseRequest(Buffer.from(\"NOT JSON\"))` → raw SyntaxError\nAfter: `parseRequest(Buffer.from(\"NOT JSON\"))` → `Error: JSON-RPC request body is not valid JSON.`",
        "branch": "fix/codex-sandbox-json-rpc-parse-guard",
